# A2ML Profile: a2ml/anchor

@abstract:
Validation profile for the ANCHOR.a2ml record — the canonical authority
identity for a repository. Non-executable; five-axis-bounded per SPEC.adoc
Section 8.2.
@end

@profile-def(id=a2ml/anchor, version="1.0.0"):
required_sections:
  - id
  - version
  - clade
  - status
allowed_directives: closed [ profile ]
required_directives: []
reference_classes: []
min_attestation: checked
@end

# Notes

@rationale:
ANCHOR is the smallest, most load-bearing 6a2 record: it asserts a repo's
canonical identity. Its dialect is key-based (top-level `key: value`), so here
`required_sections` names the required top-level KEYS rather than [section]
headers. All four — `id` (canonical authority id), `version`, `clade`
(taxonomy), and `status` — are required; an anchor missing any of them cannot
serve as an authority. `ssg` and `parents` are optional relationship fields.
@end
